# Next.js + Clerk + Supabase

## Routing

- Route groups: `(public)`, `(member)`, `(admin)` — shared `GymShell` layout
- Auth pages: `sign-in/[[...sign-in]]`, `sign-up/[[...sign-up]]`
- Protected routes enforced in `src/proxy.ts` (Clerk) + `requireMember` / `requireStaff` in server code

## Proxy (`src/proxy.ts`)

- Combines Clerk `clerkMiddleware` + Supabase `updateSession` from `@/lib/supabase/session`
- Do not recreate `middleware.ts` — it is deprecated in Next.js 16

## Supabase clients

- Browser: `@/lib/supabase/client`
- Server Components / Actions: `@/lib/supabase/server`
- Key env: `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` (not legacy anon unless fallback)
- Service role: **optional**, server-only, never `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`

## Auth split

- **Clerk** — who is signed in; session token passed to Supabase via `@/lib/supabase/clerk-server`
- **Supabase third-party auth** — Clerk domain registered in Supabase Dashboard (not JWT templates)
- **Supabase + RLS** — what data they can read/write (primary enforcement)
- Map Clerk user → `profiles` → `gym_memberships.role` for RBAC helpers in app code

## Migrations & CLI

- Create: `supabase migration new <name>` → edit SQL in `supabase/migrations/`
- Apply local: `supabase db reset` · Apply remote: `supabase db push`
- Run these yourself — do not defer to the user. Full checklist: `.cursor/rules/supabase-cli-rls.mdc`

## Data writes

- Prefer Server Actions with Zod validation
- Demo mode uses `src/lib/demo-data.ts` until Supabase queries replace it
- New tables: migration + **RLS enabled** + policies for select/insert/update/delete as needed

## UI

- Responsive strategy by route group — see `.cursor/rules/responsive-design.mdc`
- Public, member, staff, and trainer surfaces: mobile-first, large tap targets, minimal clutter
- Owner settings / CMS: desktop-first, reasonably usable on mobile
- Reuse `Button`, `Card`, `Input` from `src/components/ui/`
- Domain components: `leaderboards/`, `pr/`, `competitions/`, `admin/`, `social/`
